# ChatGPT Usability Testing for Elderly / Low‑Tech Users

**Project goal:** Simulate how an elderly person (70+ years, limited tech experience) would interact with ChatGPT. Identify usability issues, confusing UI elements, and response clarity problems.

**QA role:** Manual testing, test case design, defect reporting, accessibility thinking.

**Tools:** ChatGPT (web & mobile), screen reader simulation (basic), large‑font mode.

**Key findings summary:**
- Elderly users struggle with small UI elements and ambiguous button labels.
- Long answers cause confusion – need “stop response” button clearly marked.
- Voice input is preferred but not always reliable.

**Repository contents:**
- `/test-cases` – 5 manual test cases written for elderly persona.
- `/bug-reports` – Sample defect reports with severity/priority.
- `test-summary.md` – Metrics and observations.
- `elderly-feedback-template.md` – Template for collecting user feedback.

**Author:** Heba Nasser – ISTQB Certified Tester, QA Engineer 
[GitHub Profile](https://github.com/heba-nasser)
```

